US-001 is complete. All acceptance criteria met.

## What changed

**`auth.config.ts`** — the `session` callback no longer copies `inventoryApiKey`/`inventoryLocationId`. The `jwt` callback still stores both in the token, which travels encrypted.

**`types/next-auth.d.ts`** — both fields removed from `Session`, kept in `User` (feeds the `jwt` callback) and `JWT`. This is what made the change verifiable: `tsc` pinpointed the single remaining consumer.

**`lib/inventoryClient.ts`** — that consumer was `getInventoryConfig()`, which read the credential straight off the session. It now resolves it server-side from the `organizations` table using the session's `organizationId`, preserving the existing env-var fallback for super_admins and orgs without a stored credential.

## Verification

Typecheck, lint, build, and 85 tests all pass (8 new). For AC 5 I ran the dev server, logged in, and hit the endpoint:

```
GET /api/auth/session
{"user":{"name":"Admin","email":"admin@example.com","id":"616ac95f-…","role":"admin",
  "organizationId":"bb07c46f-…","organizationName":"tiendita",
  "organizationStatus":"active","organizationPlan":"basic"},"expires":"…"}
```

One caveat worth stating plainly: every organization in the local dev DB has a `null` `inventory_api_key`, so "no string starting with `inv_live_`" would have passed even before this change. What the output above actually proves is the stronger property — the fields are absent from the payload entirely. `auth.config.test.ts` covers the literal AC by running the real callbacks over a user carrying an `inv_live_` key and asserting it never reaches the serialized session.

`/profile`, `/products`, and `/sell` all render 200 through the new resolution path. The inventory service wasn't running, so its API calls fail as they did before — not a regression.

Two notes for the next iteration: no commits were made, per the workflow. And the dev server had to run on a non-default port — something in Cursor holds `127.0.0.1:3000`, which pushes `next dev` onto 3001, the port `INVENTORY_API_URL` expects. Worth passing `-p` explicitly when verifying against the real service.

